navigate() only knew nine pages
==============================

The Daemons page existed, had a nav entry, had a group and an icon, and clicking it did nothing. The
router holds a hardcoded allow-list:

    let pages = ["new", "chat", "search", "projects", "project", "artifacts",
                 "schedules", "tools", "settings"];
    if (!pages.includes(page)) page = "new";

`daemons` was never in it, so every navigation fell through to the composer with no error anywhere —
the click landed, the handler ran, and the page quietly reset. Added.

This is the second time this session that a feature looked broken because a list elsewhere never heard
about it (the first was the automation bridge that nothing defined). A page is not wired until the
router knows its name.
diff -Naur -x target -x '*.rlib' -x '*.rmeta' /tmp/mk35/a46/resources/ui/app.js /tmp/mk35/b/resources/ui/app.js
--- a/resources/ui/app.js
+++ b/resources/ui/app.js
@@ -380,6 +380,7 @@
       "project",
       "artifacts",
       "schedules",
+      "daemons",
       "tools",
       "settings",
     ];
